a show of force by Congolese soldiers as  they take us to their defense positions  against the Allied democratic forces  rebel group or ADF deep in the forest  the Army has sent five generals to  command 22,000 soldiers in the fight  against an estimated 2,000 ADF fighters  on the run in the jungle  the generals discussed strategy and  visit troops on the front line we are  dealing with terrorists they are now  unable to fight the military so they go  back and kill civilians but will not  stop until they leave United Nations  officials say the rebels are holding  hundreds of hostages kidnapped in the  last year and a half the area was formed  in western Uganda in the 1990s with the  aim of creating an Islamic state the  Ugandan army forced the fighters to move  to neighbouring DRC where they were  initially tolerated the aims of ADF  aren't clear but they attacked and  robbed villages like this one with guns  and machetes  to cut their victims to pieces this is  the last village before you get to areas  in the forest where the military is  fighting ADF people here have told us  that they had been terrorized by the  group for so long and army commanders  we've talked to say that soldiers have  been able to push the group farther into  the forest they have killed many of them  including some commanders another group  is very much on the run some Congolese  say the military is using a local armed  group called my mine to help fight the  ADF army commanders we talked to denied  that some mai-mai factions have been  accused of human rights abuses in remote  villages they control this woman says a  mime i arrested her and five other women  who were accused of attempting to poison  someone in the community I told him I  did not try to poison anyone but they  will not believe me they were beating us  badly I decided to run they shot me  doctors had to amputate one of my legs  UN peacekeepers say they have increased  patrols in villages and are providing  tactical and logistical support to the  Congolese army - you got these ATF  rubles sometimes attack villages that  are close to military bases and  positions what surprising people think  security forces aren't doing enough  either they are disorganized or their  strategy to defeat ATF is not working  nearly 1,000 Congolese villagers have  been killed by ADF since the military  offensive against the group started in  October victims we talked to say they  just want the attacks to stop Catholics  or al jazeera bene in the eastern  Democratic Republic of Congo
 

